.TH "NOTIFICATION.MAXACTIONS_STATIC" "3JS" "May 31, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Notification.maxActions_static \- Notification: maxActions static
property
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]maxActions\f[B]\f[R] read\-only static property of the
\f[CR]Notification\f[R] interface returns the maximum number of actions
that can be displayed in a notification.
.SH VALUE
An integer.
.SH DESCRIPTION
Notification actions are buttons or controls that appear within
persistent notifications.
Actions are set using the \f[CR]actions\f[R] option of the second
argument of the \f[CR]showNotification()\f[R] method.
.PP
Browsers typically limit the maximum number of actions they will display
for a particular notification.
The \f[CR]maxActions\f[R] property returns that limit, which is the
maximum number of elements in the \f[CR]Notification.actions\f[R] array
that will be respected by the user agent.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Log the maximum possible number of actions
The following snippet logs the maximum number of supported actions.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] maxActions = Notification.maxActions;
console.log(
  \(gaThis device can display at most ${maxActions} actions on each notification.\(ga,
);
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
Using the Notifications API
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]Notification.actions\f[R]
